begin model
#@model_id: m01_exp_decay
#@title: First-order exponential decay (PyBNF recovery fixture)
#@description: S' = -k*S. Single species degrades with rate constant k.
#@source: trimmed from BNGL_library/m01_exp_decay.bngl for the recovery test tier
#
# Recovery-tier conventions (see tests/test_recovery_m01.py):
#   * The fitted rate constant uses PyBNF's canonical alias form ``k k__FREE``:
#     the model parameter ``k`` references the free parameter ``k__FREE`` (whose
#     value PyBNF injects per evaluation). BNG2.pl preserves this as a .net
#     ConstantExpression that bngsim re-evaluates when k__FREE is set, so the
#     optimizer's changes flow through to the reaction rate. This is a one-line
#     diff from the library source (``k 0.3`` -> ``k k__FREE``).
#   * A single ODE simulate action (the ssa/nf actions from the library model
#     are dropped) keeps the fit deterministic and fast.

begin parameters
  k        k__FREE   # 1/s  decay rate constant (fitted via free param k__FREE)
  S_init   10        # molecules  initial count of S (fixed/known)
end parameters

begin molecule types
  S()
end molecule types

begin seed species
  S()  S_init
end seed species

begin observables
  Molecules  Obs_Tot_S  S()
end observables

begin reaction rules
  S() -> 0  k
end reaction rules

end model

begin actions
  generate_network({overwrite=>1})
  simulate({method=>"ode",suffix=>"ode",t_start=>0,t_end=>20,n_steps=>20})
end actions
